    "body": "Critical Risk Team partner George McLeod.\nPosted By: Adrian Pocobelli November 25, 2026\nThis week’s episode features George McLeod , partner at Critical Risk Team, in conversation with host Adrian Pocobelli about U.S. overtures to Myanmar and their implications for the heavy rare earths trade. McLeod explains why he expects Myanmar’s heavy rare earths to keep flowing to China despite recent U.S. efforts.\nHe also discusses security risks facing miners in Mexico and why he thinks some companies will begin to pull out of the country.\nIn this week’s Spotlight, PearTree Canada founder and CEO Ron Bernbaum discusses what Canada’s newly passed federal budget could mean for the mining sector and what Ottawa could do to encourage more resource development.\nAll this and more with host Adrian Pocobelli.\n“Rattlesnake Railroad”, “Big Western Sky”, “Western Adventure” and “Battle on the Western Frontier” by Brett Van Donsel ( ⁠www.incompetech.com⁠ ).\nLicensed under Creative Commons: By Attribution 4.0 License\n⁠creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0⁠\nApple Podcasts: ⁠ https://podcasts.apple.com/ca/podcast/the-northern-miner-podcast/id1099281201⁠\nSpotify: ⁠ https://open.spotify.com/show/78lyjMTRlRwZxQwz2fwQ4K⁠\nYouTube: ⁠ https://www.youtube.com/@NorthernMiner⁠\nSoundcloud: ⁠ https://soundcloud.com/northern-miner\nThe Northern Miner · Myanmar’s heavy rare earths will keep flowing to China, ft George McLeod\nPrint\nTAG: Podcast\nRepublish this article",
